From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: unisolver <patches@unisolver.invalid>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 21:54:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mmap pattern store

Pattern tables can be memory-mapped from a UNISOLV2 container instead of
being deserialized into a Vec: a deep database stays on disk and pages in
on demand (resident memory 1.1 GB -> about 120 MB). save_to_file_v2 writes
the container; load_from_file recognizes its magic and otherwise defers to
from_bytes. For mapped tables a bounds check at probe time in
pattern_search replaces the whole-table validate sweep.

